  "distributed-locking-idempotency-amp-safe-retries.md": "# Distributed Locking, Idempotency &amp; Safe Retries\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Distributed Locking, Idempotency &amp; Safe Retries**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Distributed lock use cases \u2014 prevent double-processing, inventory decrement\n- Redlock \u2014 Redis-based algorithm using quorum of N nodes\n- ZooKeeper / etcd for distributed coordination (more robust than Redlock)\n- Optimistic locking (version columns) \u2014 retry on conflict, no lock held\n\n---\n\n## Distributed lock use cases \u2014 prevent double-processing, inventory decrement\n\nDetailed content for **Distributed lock use cases \u2014 prevent double-processing, inventory decrement** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Redlock \u2014 Redis-based algorithm using quorum of N nodes\n\nDetailed content for **Redlock \u2014 Redis-based algorithm using quorum of N nodes** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## ZooKeeper / etcd for distributed coordination (more robust than Redlock)\n\nDetailed content for **ZooKeeper / etcd for distributed coordination (more robust than Redlock)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Optimistic locking (version columns) \u2014 retry on conflict, no lock held\n\nDetailed content for **Optimistic locking (version columns) \u2014 retry on conflict, no lock held** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
