  "dns-load-balancers-amp-traffic-routing.md": "# DNS, Load Balancers &amp; Traffic Routing\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **DNS, Load Balancers &amp; Traffic Routing**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- DNS resolution: recursive resolver \u2192 root \u2192 TLD \u2192 authoritative\n- DNS record types: A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT, NS\n- GeoDNS / latency-based routing (Route 53 / Cloudflare)\n- L4 (TCP) load balancer \u2014 fast, blind to HTTP content\n- L7 (HTTP) load balancer \u2014 URL routing, sticky sessions, header inspection\n- LB algorithms: round robin, least-conn, IP hash, consistent hash, weighted\n- Health checks \u2014 active (ping) vs passive (track error rates)\n- Reverse proxy \u2014 single ingress, SSL termination, request buffering\n\n---\n\n## DNS resolution: recursive resolver \u2192 root \u2192 TLD \u2192 authoritative\n\nDetailed content for **DNS resolution: recursive resolver \u2192 root \u2192 TLD \u2192 authoritative** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## DNS record types: A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT, NS\n\nDetailed content for **DNS record types: A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT, NS** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## GeoDNS / latency-based routing (Route 53 / Cloudflare)\n\nDetailed content for **GeoDNS / latency-based routing (Route 53 / Cloudflare)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## L4 (TCP) load balancer \u2014 fast, blind to HTTP content\n\nDetailed content for **L4 (TCP) load balancer \u2014 fast, blind to HTTP content** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## L7 (HTTP) load balancer \u2014 URL routing, sticky sessions, header inspection\n\nDetailed content for **L7 (HTTP) load balancer \u2014 URL routing, sticky sessions, header inspection** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## LB algorithms: round robin, least-conn, IP hash, consistent hash, weighted\n\nDetailed content for **LB algorithms: round robin, least-conn, IP hash, consistent hash, weighted** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Health checks \u2014 active (ping) vs passive (track error rates)\n\nDetailed content for **Health checks \u2014 active (ping) vs passive (track error rates)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Reverse proxy \u2014 single ingress, SSL termination, request buffering\n\nDetailed content for **Reverse proxy \u2014 single ingress, SSL termination, request buffering** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
