  "event-driven-architecture.md": "# Event-Driven Architecture\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Event-Driven Architecture**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Event sourcing \u2014 state = fold(all events), full audit log, replayable\n- CQRS \u2014 separate write model (commands) from read model (queries)\n- SAGA pattern \u2014 chain of local txns + compensating actions (replaces 2PC)\n- Choreography (events) vs Orchestration (central coordinator)\n- Transactional Outbox \u2014 atomically write DB + outbox row, publish separately\n\n---\n\n## Event sourcing \u2014 state = fold(all events), full audit log, replayable\n\nDetailed content for **Event sourcing \u2014 state = fold(all events), full audit log, replayable** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## CQRS \u2014 separate write model (commands) from read model (queries)\n\nDetailed content for **CQRS \u2014 separate write model (commands) from read model (queries)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## SAGA pattern \u2014 chain of local txns + compensating actions (replaces 2PC)\n\nDetailed content for **SAGA pattern \u2014 chain of local txns + compensating actions (replaces 2PC)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Choreography (events) vs Orchestration (central coordinator)\n\nDetailed content for **Choreography (events) vs Orchestration (central coordinator)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Transactional Outbox \u2014 atomically write DB + outbox row, publish separately\n\nDetailed content for **Transactional Outbox \u2014 atomically write DB + outbox row, publish separately** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
  "foundational-designs.md": "# Foundational Designs\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Foundational Designs**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- URL Shortener (TinyURL/bit.ly) \u2014 hash + base62, collision handling, analytics\n- Distributed Cache (Redis cluster) \u2014 consistent hashing, eviction, replication\n- Key-Value Store \u2014 LSM tree, compaction, range queries\n- Content Delivery Network \u2014 pull vs push, origin shield, cache invalidation\n- Rate Limiter (distributed) \u2014 token bucket in Redis, per-user limits\n- Distributed Job Scheduler \u2014 priority queues, at-least-once execution, dedup\n\n---\n\n## URL Shortener (TinyURL/bit.ly) \u2014 hash + base62, collision handling, analytics\n\nDetailed content for **URL Shortener (TinyURL/bit.ly) \u2014 hash + base62, collision handling, analytics** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Distributed Cache (Redis cluster) \u2014 consistent hashing, eviction, replication\n\nDetailed content for **Distributed Cache (Redis cluster) \u2014 consistent hashing, eviction, replication** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Key-Value Store \u2014 LSM tree, compaction, range queries\n\nDetailed content for **Key-Value Store \u2014 LSM tree, compaction, range queries** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Content Delivery Network \u2014 pull vs push, origin shield, cache invalidation\n\nDetailed content for **Content Delivery Network \u2014 pull vs push, origin shield, cache invalidation** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Rate Limiter (distributed) \u2014 token bucket in Redis, per-user limits\n\nDetailed content for **Rate Limiter (distributed) \u2014 token bucket in Redis, per-user limits** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Distributed Job Scheduler \u2014 priority queues, at-least-once execution, dedup\n\nDetailed content for **Distributed Job Scheduler \u2014 priority queues, at-least-once execution, dedup** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
  "graceful-degradation-amp-load-shedding.md": "# Graceful Degradation &amp; Load Shedding\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Graceful Degradation &amp; Load Shedding**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Fallback responses \u2014 return stale cache or default when upstream is down\n- Feature flags / kill switches \u2014 turn off expensive features under load\n- Load shedding \u2014 reject low-priority requests early (return 503) before overload\n- Priority queues \u2014 critical work executes even when system is degraded\n\n---\n\n## Fallback responses \u2014 return stale cache or default when upstream is down\n\nDetailed content for **Fallback responses \u2014 return stale cache or default when upstream is down** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Feature flags / kill switches \u2014 turn off expensive features under load\n\nDetailed content for **Feature flags / kill switches \u2014 turn off expensive features under load** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Load shedding \u2014 reject low-priority requests early (return 503) before overload\n\nDetailed content for **Load shedding \u2014 reject low-priority requests early (return 503) before overload** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Priority queues \u2014 critical work executes even when system is degraded\n\nDetailed content for **Priority queues \u2014 critical work executes even when system is degraded** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
