  "logging-amp-distributed-tracing.md": "# Logging &amp; Distributed Tracing\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Logging &amp; Distributed Tracing**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Structured logs \u2014 JSON with trace_id, user_id, latency_ms on every line\n- Distributed tracing \u2014 trace_id threads requests across services (Jaeger, Zipkin)\n- W3C Trace Context standard \u2014 interoperable trace propagation headers\n- CloudTrail / Activity Log \u2014 audit trail for &#x27;who did what when&#x27;\n- Alert fatigue \u2014 every alert must be actionable or it becomes noise\n\n---\n\n## Structured logs \u2014 JSON with trace_id, user_id, latency_ms on every line\n\nDetailed content for **Structured logs \u2014 JSON with trace_id, user_id, latency_ms on every line** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Distributed tracing \u2014 trace_id threads requests across services (Jaeger, Zipkin)\n\nDetailed content for **Distributed tracing \u2014 trace_id threads requests across services (Jaeger, Zipkin)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## W3C Trace Context standard \u2014 interoperable trace propagation headers\n\nDetailed content for **W3C Trace Context standard \u2014 interoperable trace propagation headers** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## CloudTrail / Activity Log \u2014 audit trail for &#x27;who did what when&#x27;\n\nDetailed content for **CloudTrail / Activity Log \u2014 audit trail for &#x27;who did what when&#x27;** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Alert fatigue \u2014 every alert must be actionable or it becomes noise\n\nDetailed content for **Alert fatigue \u2014 every alert must be actionable or it becomes noise** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
