  "partitioning-sharding-amp-data-distribution.md": "# Partitioning, Sharding &amp; Data Distribution\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Partitioning, Sharding &amp; Data Distribution**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Range sharding \u2014 split by key ranges (e.g., ID 0-1M, 1M-2M)\n- Hash sharding \u2014 hash(key) % N. Even distribution but no range queries\n- Consistent hashing \u2014 resharding moves only 1/N keys\n- Hot key problem \u2014 celebrity users, time-based skew, fix with salting\n- Cross-shard joins \u2014 expensive, avoid by denormalizing or keeping related data together\n\n---\n\n## Range sharding \u2014 split by key ranges (e.g., ID 0-1M, 1M-2M)\n\nDetailed content for **Range sharding \u2014 split by key ranges (e.g., ID 0-1M, 1M-2M)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Hash sharding \u2014 hash(key) % N. Even distribution but no range queries\n\nDetailed content for **Hash sharding \u2014 hash(key) % N. Even distribution but no range queries** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Consistent hashing \u2014 resharding moves only 1/N keys\n\nDetailed content for **Consistent hashing \u2014 resharding moves only 1/N keys** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Hot key problem \u2014 celebrity users, time-based skew, fix with salting\n\nDetailed content for **Hot key problem \u2014 celebrity users, time-based skew, fix with salting** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Cross-shard joins \u2014 expensive, avoid by denormalizing or keeping related data together\n\nDetailed content for **Cross-shard joins \u2014 expensive, avoid by denormalizing or keeping related data together** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
