  "rate-limiting-algorithms.md": "# Rate Limiting Algorithms\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Rate Limiting Algorithms**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Token bucket \u2014 refill at fixed rate, allow bursts\n- Leaky bucket \u2014 smooth output rate, no bursts\n- Fixed window \u2014 count per window, spike at window boundary\n- Sliding window log / counter \u2014 accurate, more memory\n- Distributed rate limiting with Redis (Redlock / Lua scripts)\n\n---\n\n## Token bucket \u2014 refill at fixed rate, allow bursts\n\nDetailed content for **Token bucket \u2014 refill at fixed rate, allow bursts** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Leaky bucket \u2014 smooth output rate, no bursts\n\nDetailed content for **Leaky bucket \u2014 smooth output rate, no bursts** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Fixed window \u2014 count per window, spike at window boundary\n\nDetailed content for **Fixed window \u2014 count per window, spike at window boundary** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Sliding window log / counter \u2014 accurate, more memory\n\nDetailed content for **Sliding window log / counter \u2014 accurate, more memory** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Distributed rate limiting with Redis (Redlock / Lua scripts)\n\nDetailed content for **Distributed rate limiting with Redis (Redlock / Lua scripts)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
  "real-time-communication-polling-sse-websockets-amp-webrtc.md": "# Real-Time Communication: Polling, SSE, WebSockets &amp; WebRTC\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Real-Time Communication: Polling, SSE, WebSockets &amp; WebRTC**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Short polling \u2014 client requests every N seconds, wasteful\n- Long polling \u2014 server holds connection until data ready or timeout\n- SSE (Server-Sent Events) \u2014 HTTP-based, server\u2192client only, auto-reconnect\n- WebSockets \u2014 full-duplex TCP, use for chat, real-time games, collaboration\n- WebRTC \u2014 peer-to-peer media, used for video calls (Zoom, Meet)\n- Scaling WebSockets \u2014 sticky LB or message broker fan-out (Redis Pub/Sub)\n\n---\n\n## Short polling \u2014 client requests every N seconds, wasteful\n\nDetailed content for **Short polling \u2014 client requests every N seconds, wasteful** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Long polling \u2014 server holds connection until data ready or timeout\n\nDetailed content for **Long polling \u2014 server holds connection until data ready or timeout** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## SSE (Server-Sent Events) \u2014 HTTP-based, server\u2192client only, auto-reconnect\n\nDetailed content for **SSE (Server-Sent Events) \u2014 HTTP-based, server\u2192client only, auto-reconnect** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## WebSockets \u2014 full-duplex TCP, use for chat, real-time games, collaboration\n\nDetailed content for **WebSockets \u2014 full-duplex TCP, use for chat, real-time games, collaboration** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## WebRTC \u2014 peer-to-peer media, used for video calls (Zoom, Meet)\n\nDetailed content for **WebRTC \u2014 peer-to-peer media, used for video calls (Zoom, Meet)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Scaling WebSockets \u2014 sticky LB or message broker fan-out (Redis Pub/Sub)\n\nDetailed content for **Scaling WebSockets \u2014 sticky LB or message broker fan-out (Redis Pub/Sub)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
