  "sql-vs-nosql-decision-framework.md": "# SQL vs NoSQL Decision Framework\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **SQL vs NoSQL Decision Framework**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- SQL (RDBMS) \u2014 ACID, joins, schema, mature tooling (default pick)\n- Document stores (MongoDB, CouchDB) \u2014 flexible schema, nested objects\n- Key-Value (Redis, DynamoDB) \u2014 sub-ms lookups, cache, sessions\n- Wide-column (Cassandra, HBase, ScyllaDB) \u2014 massive write throughput, time-series\n- Graph DBs (Neo4j, Neptune) \u2014 many-to-many, fraud detection, social graphs\n- Time-series (InfluxDB, TimescaleDB) \u2014 append-heavy, retention policies, IoT metrics\n- Search engines (Elasticsearch / OpenSearch) \u2014 inverted index, full-text\n\n---\n\n## SQL (RDBMS) \u2014 ACID, joins, schema, mature tooling (default pick)\n\nDetailed content for **SQL (RDBMS) \u2014 ACID, joins, schema, mature tooling (default pick)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Document stores (MongoDB, CouchDB) \u2014 flexible schema, nested objects\n\nDetailed content for **Document stores (MongoDB, CouchDB) \u2014 flexible schema, nested objects** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Key-Value (Redis, DynamoDB) \u2014 sub-ms lookups, cache, sessions\n\nDetailed content for **Key-Value (Redis, DynamoDB) \u2014 sub-ms lookups, cache, sessions** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Wide-column (Cassandra, HBase, ScyllaDB) \u2014 massive write throughput, time-series\n\nDetailed content for **Wide-column (Cassandra, HBase, ScyllaDB) \u2014 massive write throughput, time-series** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Graph DBs (Neo4j, Neptune) \u2014 many-to-many, fraud detection, social graphs\n\nDetailed content for **Graph DBs (Neo4j, Neptune) \u2014 many-to-many, fraud detection, social graphs** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Time-series (InfluxDB, TimescaleDB) \u2014 append-heavy, retention policies, IoT metrics\n\nDetailed content for **Time-series (InfluxDB, TimescaleDB) \u2014 append-heavy, retention policies, IoT metrics** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Search engines (Elasticsearch / OpenSearch) \u2014 inverted index, full-text\n\nDetailed content for **Search engines (Elasticsearch / OpenSearch) \u2014 inverted index, full-text** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
  "storage-types-block-object-amp-file.md": "# Storage Types: Block, Object &amp; File\n\n## Overview\nWelcome to the module on **Storage Types: Block, Object &amp; File**. This page covers the following related subtopics:\n\n- Block storage (EBS, Azure Disk) \u2014 attach to one VM, high IOPS, DBs/OS disks\n- File storage (EFS, NFS, Azure Files) \u2014 multi-mount, POSIX semantics\n- Object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob) \u2014 flat namespace, infinite scale, HTTP API\n- S3 key design \u2014 prefix distribution for parallel requests (avoid sequential prefixes)\n- Distributed file system (HDFS, Ceph) \u2014 large dataset processing, MapReduce\n\n---\n\n## Block storage (EBS, Azure Disk) \u2014 attach to one VM, high IOPS, DBs/OS disks\n\nDetailed content for **Block storage (EBS, Azure Disk) \u2014 attach to one VM, high IOPS, DBs/OS disks** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## File storage (EFS, NFS, Azure Files) \u2014 multi-mount, POSIX semantics\n\nDetailed content for **File storage (EFS, NFS, Azure Files) \u2014 multi-mount, POSIX semantics** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob) \u2014 flat namespace, infinite scale, HTTP API\n\nDetailed content for **Object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob) \u2014 flat namespace, infinite scale, HTTP API** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## S3 key design \u2014 prefix distribution for parallel requests (avoid sequential prefixes)\n\nDetailed content for **S3 key design \u2014 prefix distribution for parallel requests (avoid sequential prefixes)** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n## Distributed file system (HDFS, Ceph) \u2014 large dataset processing, MapReduce\n\nDetailed content for **Distributed file system (HDFS, Ceph) \u2014 large dataset processing, MapReduce** is currently being formulated. Check back soon!\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Teacher's Note:** This is the *Light-Depth Baseline Version* of this tutorial. We will upgrade this page with deep-dives shortly!\n",
